{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-22881","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23135","text":"PULSE × box-and-box — Arithmetic Integration Review"}]},{"id":"blk-22882","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23136","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-23137","text":" review (no schema break) · "},{"id":"spn-23138","marks":["bold"],"text":"Kernel:"},{"id":"spn-23139","text":" "},{"id":"spn-23140","marks":["code"],"text":"box-and-box"},{"id":"spn-23141","text":" v0.8.0 (8 rungs, 97 laws) "},{"id":"spn-23142","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope:"},{"id":"spn-23143","text":" how the PULSE loop-manifest standard (OS-010) relates to the [&] governance kernel, what already aligns, and what additive wiring is available."}]},{"id":"blk-22883","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23144","text":"TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-22884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23145","text":"PULSE and box-and-box are "},{"id":"spn-23146","marks":["bold"],"text":"orthogonal and complementary"},{"id":"spn-23147","text":". PULSE "},{"id":"spn-23148","marks":["italic"],"text":"sequences a loop over time"},{"id":"spn-23149","text":" (phases, cadence, substrates, cross-loop signals). box-and-box renders a "},{"id":"spn-23150","marks":["bold"],"text":"single-decision verdict"},{"id":"spn-23151","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-23152","marks":["code"],"text":"feasible ▸ permitted ▸ best"},{"id":"spn-23153","text":" over an un-weakenable safety floor. The kernel governs "},{"id":"spn-23154","marks":["italic"],"text":"what is allowed to happen at"},{"id":"spn-23155","text":" a PULSE phase; it is not itself a phase or a set of phases. There is "},{"id":"spn-23156","marks":["bold"],"text":"no 1:1 mapping"},{"id":"spn-23157","text":" between the 8 rungs and the 5 phase kinds — do not introduce one."}]},{"id":"blk-22885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23158","text":"The integration surface is small and entirely additive:"}]},{"id":"blk-22886","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23159","text":"PULSE's 7 boolean "},{"id":"spn-23160","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-23161","text":" are the manifest-level shadow of the kernel's alethic"}]}],"id":"blk-22887","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-22889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23162","marks":["bold"],"text":"Value families"},{"id":"spn-23163","text":". They can be "},{"id":"spn-23164","marks":["italic"],"text":"checked"},{"id":"spn-23165","text":" by the kernel but the schema needs no change."}]},{"id":"blk-22890","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23166","marks":["code"],"text":"closure.guarantee"},{"id":"spn-23167","text":" is already an LTL fragment — it lines up with the kernel's"}]}],"id":"blk-22891","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-22893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23168","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal"},{"id":"spn-23169","text":" rung (rung 4) operators."}]},{"id":"blk-22894","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23170","text":"PULSE V0.2's proposed linear/affine token typing is the kernel's "},{"id":"spn-23171","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource"},{"id":"spn-23172","text":" rung"}]}],"id":"blk-22895","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-22897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23173","text":"(rung 8, the affine ledger) viewed at the manifest layer."}]},{"id":"blk-22898","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23174","text":"A loop "},{"id":"spn-23175","marks":["italic"],"text":"may"},{"id":"spn-23176","text":" declare a phase whose body is \"run the kernel verdict\" — but PULSE does not"}]}],"id":"blk-22899","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-22901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23177","text":"need a new phase "},{"id":"spn-23178","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-23179","text":" to express this; it is an ordinary "},{"id":"spn-23180","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-23181","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-23182","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-23183","text":" phase."}]},{"id":"blk-22902","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23184","text":"Rung-by-rung alignment"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22904","spans":[{"id":"spn-23185","text":"Kernel rung"}]},{"id":"blk-22905","spans":[{"id":"spn-23186","text":"PULSE construct that already carries it"}]},{"id":"blk-22906","spans":[{"id":"spn-23187","text":"Already aligned?"}]}],"id":"blk-22903","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22907","spans":[{"id":"spn-23188","text":"1. alethic ("},{"id":"spn-23189","marks":["code"],"text":"value"},{"id":"spn-23190","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-22908","spans":[{"id":"spn-23191","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-23192","text":" booleans (π/κ/β/σ families); "},{"id":"spn-23193","marks":["code"],"text":"phase.kind"},{"id":"spn-23194","text":" enumerates what "},{"id":"spn-23195","marks":["italic"],"text":"can"},{"id":"spn-23196","text":" happen"}]},{"id":"blk-22909","spans":[{"id":"spn-23197","text":"✅ at manifest level"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22910","spans":[{"id":"spn-23198","text":"2. axiological ("},{"id":"spn-23199","marks":["code"],"text":"score"},{"id":"spn-23200","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-22911","spans":[{"id":"spn-23201","text":"— (PULSE does not rank; PRISM does)"}]},{"id":"blk-22912","spans":[{"id":"spn-23202","text":"n/a — lives in PRISM"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22913","spans":[{"id":"spn-23203","text":"3. deontic (norm/govern)"}]},{"id":"blk-22914","spans":[{"id":"spn-23204","marks":["code"],"text":"substrates.policy"},{"id":"spn-23205","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23206","marks":["code"],"text":"substrates.audit"},{"id":"spn-23207","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-23208","marks":["code"],"text":"quorum_before_commit"}]},{"id":"blk-22915","spans":[{"id":"spn-23209","text":"◻ partial — declared, not enforced by 