nel's "},{"id":"spn-23310","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource"},{"id":"spn-23311","text":" rung — the affine ledger where a token is either "},{"id":"spn-23312","marks":["italic"],"text":"depletable"},{"id":"spn-23313","text":" (linear: consumed once) or "},{"id":"spn-23314","marks":["italic"],"text":"reusable"},{"id":"spn-23315","text":" (affine/\"of-course\": intact after use). "},{"id":"spn-23316","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-23317","text":" when V0.2 lands, name this correspondence explicitly and reuse the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-23318","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-23319","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23320","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-23321","text":" annihilation on overspend) rather than inventing a parallel one. The kernel's "},{"id":"spn-23322","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-23323","text":" (laws "},{"id":"spn-23324","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-23325","text":", "},{"id":"spn-23326","marks":["code"],"text":"CB1–CB3"},{"id":"spn-23327","text":") is the reference semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-22974","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23328","text":"4. An optional \"verify\" gate is just an ordinary phase"}]},{"id":"blk-22975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23329","text":"A loop that wants the kernel to gate a commit declares a normal "},{"id":"spn-23330","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-23331","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-23332","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-23333","text":" phase whose body calls "},{"id":"spn-23334","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.select(...)"},{"id":"spn-23335","text":". PULSE needs "},{"id":"spn-23336","marks":["bold"],"text":"no new phase kind"},{"id":"spn-23337","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-23338","marks":["bold"],"text":"no schema change"},{"id":"spn-23339","text":" — the verdict is a phase "},{"id":"spn-23340","marks":["italic"],"text":"body"},{"id":"spn-23341","text":", and its result is an ordinary "},{"id":"spn-23342","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-23343","text":" (or a "},{"id":"spn-23344","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationResult"},{"id":"spn-23345","text":" when κ>0). Keep the 5 canonical phase kinds intact."}]},{"id":"blk-22976","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23346","text":"What this review deliberately does NOT do"}]},{"id":"blk-22977","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23347","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-23348","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-23349","text":" add an 8th invariant, a verdict phase kind, or any required field — the"}]}],"id":"blk-22978","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22980","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23350","text":"v0.1 schema is unchanged and remains backward compatible."}]},{"id":"blk-22981","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23351","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-23352","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-23353","text":" claim a rung↔phase-kind bijection (the two are orthogonal axes)."}]}],"id":"blk-22982","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23354","text":"Enforcement of the deontic/strategic/reflexive rungs stays in the runtime that "},{"id":"spn-23355","marks":["italic"],"text":"hosts"}]}],"id":"blk-22984","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23356","text":"the loop (Delegatic for policy/audit), not in the manifest."}]},{"id":"blk-22987","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-23357","text":"Follow-ups (out of scope here)"}]},{"id":"blk-22988","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-23358","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-23359","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-conformance"},{"id":"spn-23360","text":" checker that lifts "},{"id":"spn-23361","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-23362","text":" → 